        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add gated Claw publication and validation",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Enables authenticated `family: \"claw\"` publication only when `CLAWHUB_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS=1`.\n- Validates exact package identity, canonical `CLAW.md` or JSON compatibility input, referenced sidecars, portable paths, and the shared strict manifest before release insertion.\n- Persists the validated manifest plus safe summary through existing ownership, moderation, scanning, and artifact pipelines.\n- Adds CLI detection, dry-run/publish authoring support, and operator documentation.\n- Makes this publication slice independently fail closed: stored Claws are omitted from existing public lists/search/detail/version reads while disabled, and full extracted manifests are never returned by public release serializers.\n\n## Stack\n\n- RFC: openclaw/rfcs#27\n- Depends on: #3089\n- This is ClawHub PR 2 of 4 and remains draft/experimental.\n- #3091 adds explicit Claw discovery filters and safe summary API projection; it is no longer required to close the publication security boundary.\n\n## Contract\n\nClaws remain ordinary immutable ClawHub package archives with `package.json.openclaw.claw` pointing to a safe package-relative manifest. One leading UTF-8 BOM is ignored only for `CLAW.md` frontmatter recognition; archive bytes remain unchanged for artifact integrity. A suffix-only filename such as `NOTCLAW.md` is not treated as the canonical Markdown format.\n\nThe CLI and backend carry synchronized validators. Publication cannot bypass existing owner authorization, moderation, scanning, package size, archive safety, or immutable artifact rules.\n\nThe feature gate is checked both before publication and at final insertion. Existing generic public reads also call the same gate and return no Claw while disabled, including previously stored records. Public release objects strip `extractedClawManifest`; later APIs may expose only `clawManifestSummary`.\n\n## Validation\n\n- 317 focused schema, package publication, visibility, named-read, list, and serializer tests pass.\n- All 74 ClawHub CLI package command tests pass, including Claw detection/dry-run/publish.\n- `bun run ci:types-build` passes across root, schema, CLI/admin, Convex consumers, and production build.\n- `bun run ci:static` passes.\n- Shared and standalone CLI validators are byte-for-byte synchronized for `claws.ts` and `clawPackage.ts`.\n- `git diff --check` passes.\n- `codex review --base fork/user/giodl/clawhub-claws-schema`: no actionable regression.\n\n## Proof boundary\n\nThe focused backend proof exercises enabled publication data, disabled unfiltered lists, disabled detail/version reads, enabled safe release output, and stripping of the full extracted manifest. No reusable local Convex deployment is configured in the available worktrees, so this PR does not claim a live hosted publish. The published-package cross-repo lifecycle proof remains in #3092 and should be considered part of the coordinated experimental stack review.\n\n## Stack note\n\nKeep `CLAWHUB_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS` disabled in deployments until the full reviewed stack is present. Nothing here was merged.",
